# Example Duply PRE hook — dump Postgres before the file backup runs.
#
# In your Duply profile (e.g. /etc/duply/voctoweb/conf):
#
#   PRE="nice /srv/voctoweb/bin/docker-prod-backup-db"
#   SOURCE='/var/backups/voctoweb'
#
# Or append the dump dir to an existing SOURCE that already covers /srv:
#
#   SOURCE='/srv/voctoweb/docker/production /var/backups/voctoweb'
#
# Notes:
# - Prefer the custom-format dump over backing up the raw Postgres volume.
# - Elasticsearch and Redis need no backup for cutover-style recovery
#   (reindex + empty redis). CDN files stay on the CDN.
# - Run Duply as a user that can talk to Docker (group `docker`) and write
#   BACKUP_DIR (default /var/backups/voctoweb).
# - Optional: BACKUP_DIR=/other/path BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=30 in the environment.
